Z||000000||Smoooooth GT||06-06-2001||12:34 AM||||my 5.7L the oil pressure will dop to about 8lbs at idle in drive, after driving 20-30 minutes... has plenty of oil. Oil pump??  what else could it be??  Thank's Steve<P>------------------<BR>aka..FieroSEt<BR>Fiero_87GT@yahoo.com<BR>cell.. 903 445 0849<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_6.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||06-06-2001||01:25 AM||||What's your idle speed, 600?<BR>If not and your 850 and up, go for a new pump after checking manual pressure. I hope this wasn't all of a sudden, or you may be loosing a main.||||reg||1
Z||000002||EdsB52||06-06-2001||01:36 AM||||Actually that's not considered too low by what I've read. Although my 94 Z-28 reads 22 at idle at around 800-900 rpm. At driving rpm it reads about 45. Usually if your oil pressure goes when you have enough oil, it's one of 4 things.<P>1. Main/rod bearings<P>2. Oil pump<P>3. Cam bearings.<P>4. Pressure sending unit/wiring/gauge<P>I remember older Fords would create large clearances between the camshaft and bearings and dump the pressure. Usually the oil pump won't wear out first. Like the previous guy said, bump the idle and then check it. If you don't hear lifter noises, don't worry.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Smoooooth GT||06-06-2001||07:45 AM||||thank's for the replies....  the oil press is ok until the motor warm's up or should say get hot....   I do hear a small knock at idle in drive(7-8lbs of pressure). there is the same small knock when the motor is very first started most of the time, but only last a couple of minutes until oil circulates real good.<BR>OMG, I look under and see some oil that has leaked onto my crossmember section....  what about the front oil seal???  maybe loosing a little oil then getting hot that way it will start that knocking a little.... oil pressure has alway's read 33-35 lbs at driving rpm's... then come to a red light.......... then drop's like I said to 7-8 lbs.  hhmmmm...        help. Steve<P>------------------<BR>aka..FieroSEt<BR>Fiero_87GT@yahoo.com<BR>cell.. 903 445 0849<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_6.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfixit58||06-06-2001||08:23 PM||||I had a SBC motor do that and it turned out to be bad cam bearings. I let too much oil pressure leak out before it reached the top of the motor. The motor always seemed to run a little warm, too.<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||4
